# DwarfUI service-provider cleanup separation

This DwarfUI-owned plan separates feature-local overlay cleanup from
DwarfUICore service-registration removal. It was extracted from the Core
service-provider implementation checklist because the affected lifecycle and
test ownership belong to DwarfUI.

## Phase 1 - Separate DwarfUI local cleanup from service registration removal

- [ ] Audit every DwarfUI overlay and lifecycle handler that currently performs
      both feature-local cleanup and tooltip or context-menu unregistration.
      Record the local state it owns, the service registrations it owns, and
      the reload, disable, map, and world boundaries that invoke it.
- [ ] Refactor each affected overlay so its feature-local cleanup is an
      independently callable, idempotent operation that neither accesses nor
      depends on a DwarfUICore service API.
- [ ] Move tooltip and context-menu registration removal into separately named,
      idempotent operations. Ensure a failure or stale API object during
      registration removal cannot prevent feature-local cleanup.
- [ ] Make DwarfUI root teardown perform feature-local overlay cleanup before
      acquiring current namespace-bound APIs and clearing the `dwarfui`
      tooltip and context-menu namespaces.
- [ ] Remove `is_stale_api_failure()` and any broad suppression of stale API
      errors once old overlays no longer use service APIs during their local
      cleanup.
- [ ] Preserve normal explicit unregister behavior where it provides timely
      removal, while treating root namespace clearing as the authoritative
      reload and teardown cleanup boundary.
- [ ] Add focused unit coverage for ordinary DwarfUI reload, Core-then-DwarfUI
      reload, overlay disable, and local-cleanup failure. Prove local state is
      cleared exactly once, unrelated cleanup errors still surface, and an
      independent namespace remains intact.
- [ ] Add focused DwarfSpec coverage that performs an explicit Core reload
      followed by DwarfUI reload, verifies local overlay cleanup and service
      isolation, and records terminal cleanup confirmation.
- [ ] Update DwarfUI lifecycle documentation and package-contract tests to
      describe the separation between local feature cleanup and namespace
      registration removal.
- [ ] Reduce the minecart tooltip DwarfSpec to minecart behavior only. Remove
      `assert_input_only_diagnostics()` and every assertion of private poller,
      presenter, render-hook, transport, generation, scheduling, or ownership
      diagnostic state.
- [ ] Remove the minecart DwarfSpec's exact per-frame poller-sampling assertion.
      Keep only waits required to observe the minecart action's visible tooltip
      behavior; retain poller cadence coverage in focused DwarfUICore tests.
- [ ] Remove the minecart DwarfSpec's dynamic tooltip mutation, pointer-update,
      pointer-leave, and consumed-input polling scenarios. Those are generic
      widget and tooltip-service behavior, not minecart route behavior.
- [ ] Remove the initial minecart action unregister/re-register cycle that tests
      the generic public tooltip API. Retain or replace only the assertion needed
      to prove the recreated minecart action is registered by its overlay.
- [ ] Remove synthetic staged-overlay setup, private render-hook access, and
      render-hook diagnostic assertions from the minecart DwarfSpec. Move or
      retain that coverage only in focused DwarfUICore rendering tests.
- [ ] Remove foreign overlay-wrapper injection, repair-order assertions, and
      foreign sentinel rendering from the minecart DwarfSpec. Keep wrapper
      recovery coverage in focused DwarfUICore hook tests.
- [ ] Remove Core-to-DwarfUI reload generation and hook-recovery assertions from
      the minecart DwarfSpec. Retain only a minecart-level reload check if it
      directly proves the reloaded route action can show its tooltip again.
- [ ] Rewrite the reduced minecart DwarfSpec around visible route-action
      discovery, static tooltip text and placement, eligibility loss, overlay
      recreation registration, and native Hauling-screen rendering. Update its
      name, helper set, and cleanup to match that narrow responsibility.

### Phase 1 completion gate

- [ ] No DwarfUI feature-local cleanup path depends on a current, old, or
      freshly acquired DwarfUICore API object.
- [ ] Explicit DwarfUI namespace clearing removes only DwarfUI service
      registrations after local cleanup, without suppressing unrelated overlay
      lifecycle failures.
- [ ] Ordinary and Core-then-DwarfUI reload preserve the existing DwarfUI
      feature behavior and every independent consumer namespace.
